course: dictionary
lesson: 9166
title: A word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Snowplough is a noun, and it has a second meaning in skiing, where it can also be a verb. Read the words around it to decide which meaning is right.
explain: «Snowploughs cannot see a fort in a snowbank by the road.» Roads and snowbanks are nearby, so here a snowplough is a big vehicle. In skiing, to snowplough means to slow down by pointing the front tips of your skis together in a V shape.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about roads, snow piles or drivers, it means the machine. If it is about skis, slopes or beginners, it means the skiing move. Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A snowplough is a vehicle or machine with a big blade at the front.
fact: The blade pushes snow off roads and paths so that cars and school buses can get through.
fact: In skiing, a snowplough is a way of slowing down by pointing the front tips of the skis together in a V shape.
fact: In the USA the word is spelled snowplow, but it means the same thing.
fact: Snowploughs cannot see small people well, and they throw out snow and grit, so keep away from them.
exercise: «Snowploughs cannot see a fort in a snowbank by the road.» What is a snowplough? | A kind of snowman | A small sled for children | A warm coat for skiing | *A vehicle with a big blade that pushes snow off roads
exercise: Beginner skiers learn the snowplough. What does it help them do? | Jump as high as possible | Ski backwards very fast | *Slow down by pointing their ski tips together in a V | Carry their poles
exercise: «Snow and ice also hide dangers from above and below: heavy snow and icicles can fall from roofs.» Find and copy one thing that can fall from roofs. | *icicles | fort | snowplough | kerb
test: A driver says, «The snowplough is clearing the road.» Which meaning is it? | A deep snowy hole | A way of slowing down on skis | A fast sledge for hills | *A machine that pushes snow off the road
test: A skier says, «I slowed down with a snowplough.» What does the skier mean? | *Slowed down by pointing the skis' front tips together in a V | Fell over in the deep snow | Skied very fast down a hill | Pushed snow off a road
exam: Why must children keep away from snowploughs? | Because snowploughs are painted bright pink | Because snowploughs only work in summer | Because snowploughs are very slow and quiet | *Because snowploughs cannot see small people well and throw out snow and grit
